# Dynamic colors (theme tokens)

Every visual color in this project must come from the theme system — never raw hex/rgb in components (except one-off SVG assets).

## Source of truth

- Tokens live in `src/config/theme.js` (`themes.light` / `themes.dark`)
- CSS fallbacks + Tailwind bridges live in `src/styles/index.css`
- `ThemeProvider` applies vars on `<html>` and toggles `data-mode`

## Do

- Use Tailwind semantic colors: `bg-foam`, `text-ink`, `text-hero-fg`, `border-line`, `bg-lagoon`, `text-copper`, …
- For gradients / Three.js / canvas, read `var(--token)` or `getComputedStyle(...).getPropertyValue('--token')`
- When adding a new color role, add it to **both** light and dark in `theme.js`, map it in `@theme` in `index.css`, then use the Tailwind name
- Prefer existing tokens before inventing new ones

## Don’t

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — breaks dark mode later
className="bg-[#f8f6ee] text-[#1c1c1c]"
style={{ color: '#0d6e6e' }}

// ✅ GOOD
className="bg-hero-cta text-craton"
className="text-lagoon"
style={{ background: 'radial-gradient(..., var(--highlight), ...)' }}
```

## Checklist for new UI

1. Pick a semantic token (or add one to light + dark)
2. Style with `bg-*` / `text-*` / `border-*` or `var(--*)`
3. Toggle light/dark in the navbar and verify contrast
4. Canvas/WebGL must listen for `craton:themechange` if colors are cached

## Common tokens

| Role | Token examples |
| --- | --- |
| Page bg / body text | `foam`, `ink` |
| Alt surface | `mist`, `ink-soft` |
| Brand / CTA | `lagoon`, `lagoon-deep`, `coral`, `copper` |
| Hero on dark | `craton`, `hero-base`, `hero-fg`, `hero-muted`, `hero-cta` |
| Borders | `line`, `line-on-dark` |
| Effects | `signal-line`, `signal-pulse`, `highlight`, `cursor` |
